    "type": "text",
    "text": "## Objective\nRun the draconic-loop skill exactly once: claim the next ROADMAP.md item (E19.84.02 deferred namespace identity/caching), implement test-first, mark done only when `cargo test --workspace` is green, then stop after one item.\n\n## Important Details\n- Loop constraints: exactly one `in_progress` at a time; `done` only when `cargo test --workspace` is green; stop after one item; do not start a second.\n- Repo: `/Users/jaredhembrow/Projects/draconic/draconic` on branch `main`; build is clean ahead of work.\n- ROADMAP row claimed: `E19.84.02 | in_progress | js | Deferred namespace identity/caching: same module's deferred ns shared across static import defer sites, re-export, and dynamic import.defer; distinct from eager ns (identity.js) | tests/test262 (allowlist + linker)`.\n- Probe flow: build with `cargo build -p draconic-test262 --bin probe --release`, then feed allowlist paths on stdin: `printf '%s\\n' \"test/language/import/import-defer/deferred-namespace-object/identity.js\" | ./target/release/probe`.\n- Test262 suite is present at `third_party/test262/`.\n- Probe already confirms **red**: `FAIL test/.../deferred-namespace-object/identity.js node exit 1 ... 'Static and dynamic` — failure occurs at the dynamic-import assertion (assert 3: `nsDeferred1 === nsDeferred4`). Static/re-export identity assertions (1–2) already pass because the linker binds all static deferred sites to one object; dynamic `import.defer` is the broken piece, plus deferred-vs-eager distinctness.\n- Manual JS-emit repro at `/tmp/dracex/out.mjs` shows the wrong shape: eager `import *` and static `import defer *` both produce `__ns0` (same object — spec says they must be distinct), and `const nsDeferred4 = await import(\"./dep.js\")` is an eager dynamic import, not the deferred namespace.\n- Spec semantics from `identity.js`: `GetModuleNamespace(module, phase)` keeps two caches per module — `[[DeferredNamespace]]` and `[[Namespace]]`; `ModuleNamespaceCreate` uses `\"Deferred Module\"` `@@toStringTag` for defer phase.\n- Existing infrastructure (from E19.55/E19.84.01, commit `d4c7d05`): `__draconic_deferred_ns(evaluate, exportNames)` Proxy helper in `crates/draconic-linker/src/lib.rs`; modules reachable only via `import defer` get lazy eval-thunk wrappers; eager modules reached also by deferred imports currently just resolve deferred users to the eager `__ns{id}` — the gap.\n- Dynamic `import.defer` currently emits plain `import(...)` in `crates/draconic-backend-js/src/emit.rs` (E19.55 fallback for Node); the linker must rewrite deferred dynamic `ImportCall`s to the shared cached deferred namespace binding.\n- Allowlist currently has `exotic-object-behavior.js`, `setup_FIXTURE.js`, `to-string-tag.js` for the deferred-namespace-object dir; `identity.js` (and its fixtures) must be added.\n- identity.js fixtures present in the suite dir: `dep_FIXTURE.js` (exports `foo=1, bar=2`), `dep-defer-ns_FIXTURE.js` (re-exports a deferred ns), `setup_FIXTURE.js` (sets `globalThis.evaluations = []`), plus `dep2_FIXTURE.js`, `deferred_ns_export_FIXTURE.js`, `json-module_FIXTURE.json`.\n- Was reading `resolve_export` / `collect_export_maps_rec` (linker lines ~640–830) and AST structure for `ImportCall`/`ImportDeclaration`/`StringLit` to plan the rewrite of dynamic deferred imports and per-module deferred namespace caching (`__deferred_ns{id}` separate from `__ns{id}`).\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Read `CONTEXT.md` and `ROADMAP.md`; confirmed next claimable item is E19.84.02.\n- Marked E19.84.02 `todo` → `in_progress` in `ROADMAP.md`.\n- Built probe (release) successfully; confirmed `identity.js` FAILs (red).\n- Ran manual CLI repro: `./target/release/draconic build --target js /tmp/dracex/main.js -o /tmp/dracex/out.mjs`; inspected emitted JS showing eager/deferred collision and eager dynamic import.\n- Identified root-cause design for the fix: per-module **distinct** cached deferred namespace binding (e.g. `__deferred_ns{id}`) shared by all static deferred sites, re-exports, and dynamic `import.defer`; eager static `import *` keeps `__ns{id}`.\n\n### Active\n- E19.84.02 is claimed `in_progress`; intended implementation sequence: add `identity.js` + fixtures to `tests/test262/allowlist.txt` → implement linker changes → rebuild probe → probe green → `cargo test --workspace` green → set ROADMAP row `done` → commit.\n- Investigation of linker internals (module graph, `resolve_export`, namespace renames, `ImportCall` AST) is partially complete; the exact splice points for dynamic `import.defer` rewriting and deferred ns binding emission are still being pinned down.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Implement the linker fix in `crates/draconic-linker/src/lib.rs`: when a module has any deferred namespace references (static `import defer *`, re-exported deferred ns, or dynamic `import.defer(…)`), emit one shared `__deferred_ns{id}` per target module (distinct from eager `__ns{id}`), backed by the existing `__draconic_deferred_ns` Proxy helper, and rewrite dynamic `import.defer`/`ImportCall { phase: Defer }` expressions in module bodies to reference that bound deferred namespace.\n2. Add `identity.js` (and its fixture files) to `tests/test262/allowlist.txt`.\n3. Rebuild probe, verify `identity.js` PASSes and existing deferred-namespace tests still PASS.\n4. Run `cargo test --workspace` (fast smoke slice) — gate for `done`.\n5. Set `E19.84.02` → `done` in ROADMAP.md, commit the work package, and **stop** (do not claim E19.84.03 or any further item).\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `ROADMAP.md`: E19.84.02 row is `in_progress` — the item under Loop.\n- `crates/draconic-linker/src/lib.rs`: main implementation target — deferred ns helper (`__draconic_deferred_ns`), eager-module computation, module body wrapping, import/namespace renames, `ImportCall` handling, `resolve_export`/`collect_export_maps_rec` (lines ~640–830) for re-export resolution.\n- `crates/draconic-backend-js/src/emit.rs` (lines ~532–544): emits