            "text": "The e19.66 test is guarded by `if (typeof ArrayBuffer.prototype.transferToImmutable === \"function\")`, so it passes on Node 26 where the API is absent.\n\nSo E19.85 requires implementing the immutable ArrayBuffer APIs. Since they're absent in Node, I need to provide a polyfill harness, similar to E19.79/E19.80. But wait — the \"runtime\" note and the js target running in Node. Polyfilling ArrayBuffer immutable semantics in JS-level harness is very complex, particularly because immutable buffers are used by typed arrays with detached/non-extensible semantics. \n\nActually, let me reconsider. The Test262 tests for these features have `features: [sharedarraybuffer, arraybuffer-transfer, immutable-arraybuffer]` and use typed arrays to write to immutable buffers expecting TypeError. A faithful polyfill would need to make typed array writes to immutable buffers throw. That's essentially impossible to do correctly purely in JS (can't intercept typed array element writes). \n\nHmm. So a JS polyfill can't correctly implement immutable ArrayBuffer semantics because once a typed array's buffer is immutable, writes should throw, and you can't override typed array element set in JS.\n\nWait — unless the Draconic runtime is not just Node. Let me reconsider. Actually, the js backend emits JS that runs in Node. So the \"runtime\" is Node. The immutable APIs need to exist for the Test262 tests to pass. If Node doesn't have them, and we can't faithfully polyfill...\n\nBut E19.79/E19.80 added polyfills for Error.isError and Math.sumPrecise which ARE faithfully polyfillable in pure JS. For ArrayBuffer immutable, they're not really.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider what exactly the tests assert. Let me check what Test262 tests exist for `.immutable`, `transferToImmutable`, `sliceToImmutable`. Let me look in the test262 suite.\n\nActually, maybe I should reconsider the scope. Let me look at what the allowlist currently contains and check the actual Test262 tests for these features. Maybe the tests just assert property descriptors, and \"immutable\" is a boolean property, and transferToImmutable/sliceToImmutable create detached buffers. \n\nLet me check the third_party test262 suite for these files.",
