            "text": "Now I have a clear picture of the test files. None of the three method dirs' tests require writing to an *immutable* buffer (typed-array write enforcement). They:\n- create immutable buffers via transferToImmutable/sliceToImmutable, then READ from them (`new Uint8Array(dest)`) and compare.\n- Tests that write to immutable buffers is under ArrayBuffer/prototype/transfer, resize, etc. — NOT in scope.\n\nSo a JS polyfill that returns a real (mutable) ArrayBuffer from transferToImmutable/sliceToImmutable would make reads work, and `.immutable` getter returns true via a WeakSet. Since no test in scope writes to an immutable buffer, the inability to enforce write-semantics is not exercised by the in-scope tests. \n\nKey requirements to implement faithfully in the polyfill:\n1. `.immutable` accessor getter on ArrayBuffer.prototype — returns true iff buffer in immutable WeakSet; false otherwise; getter name \"get immutable\", length 0; accessor property descriptor (get present, set undefined, enumerable false, configurable true). Also must throw TypeError for wrong receivers (non-object, shared arraybuffer, no [[ArrayBufferData]]). Requires InternalSlot check — we can approximate by `this instanceof ArrayBuffer` and detect SharedArrayBuffer via `this instanceof SharedArrayBuffer`.\n2. `transferToImmutable(newLength?)` — detaches `this`, returns an immutable buffer with `maxByteLength === byteLength` (i.e., not resizable), `byteLength === resolved`, contents copied. Also must handle: same-or-smaller copies prefix, larger copies + zero-fills rest. newLength coercion via ToIndex. Not a constructor. length = 0? Let me check prop-desc for transferToImmutable length/name. Actually spec: length is 0 (optional arg). name = \"transferToImmutable\".\n3. `sliceToImmutable(start, end)` — like slice but returns immutable buffer. Copies [from,to). length 2, name \"sliceToImmutable\".\n\nConstraints for faithful behavior:\n- `transferToImmutable` must actually DETACH the source. In Node, `source.transfer(newLength)` detaches it and returns a new buffer — but the new buffer would be resizable... actually Node's `transfer` returns a non-resizable? In Node, `ab.transfer()` returns a new ArrayBuffer with same length, and ab becomes detached. We can use `structuredClone` with transfer, or `buffer.transfer()` (Node 20.14+). Node 26 supports `buffer.transfer()`. Then we need to make it \"immutable\" — meaning return object whose `.immutable` getter returns true and resizable false. But a normal Node ArrayBuffer has `.resizable === false` already (non-resizable). And `.maxByteLength === byteLength`. And `.detached` false. So a normal transferred buffer already satisfies resizable:false, maxByteLength==byteLength, byteLength correct. We just need `.immutable` to return true → track in WeakSet.\n\nBut there's subtlety: `to-larger.js` transfers to larger length, expects the returned buffer's byteLength = larger, with zero-filled tail, and `.immutable`, `.resizable false`, `.maxByteLength === resolvedNewLength`. A Node `source.transfer(larger)` gives byteLength=larger, zero-filled tail. Then track as immutable.\n\nAlso slicing: `return-immutable.js` does `$DETACHBUFFER(ab); assert ab.immutable === false`. Fine.\n\nBut important: the polyfill returns a NEW real ArrayBuffer from these methods, so `new Uint8Array(dest)` works and reads correct content. Good.\n\nNow, the biggest subtlety: faithful `sliceToImmutable` must NOT detach the source (it's a copy, source stays). And `this-becomes-detached.js` requires: if source gets detached by side effects during argument coercion (end.valueOf calls $DETACHBUFFER(ab)), then throw TypeError and NOT throw before reading args — must coerce start then end first, then check detach. So ordering: coerce start & end, THEN if detached throw. Actually spec: ResolveBounds coerces start, end, and if during that the buffer detached, then step 11 throws TypeError.\n\nLet me carefully implement to match spec ordering:\n- RequireInternalSlot (this is ArrayBuffer & not SharedArrayBuffer)\n- If detached → TypeError (this-is-not-detached: detached before reading args → calls should be empty → so detach check must happen BEFORE coercing start/end!). Wait, this-is-not-detached.js: detached buffer, then `detached.sliceToImmutable(objStart, objEnd)` → assert.throws TypeError, calls must be [] (args not read). So YES: check detached first, before coercion. Good.\n\nAnd this-becomes-detached.js: non-detached source; objEnd.valueOf detaches it. sliceToImmutable should coerce start (start.valueOf), then end (end.valueOf detaches), then throw TypeError because now detached. So order: coerce start, coerce end, then if detached throw TypeError. And calls = [start, end].\n\nSo the logic:\n```\nsliceToImmutable(start, end):\n  RequireInternalSlot; if shared → TypeError; if detached → TypeError (before coercion)\n  let len = this.byteLength\n  coerce start (ToIntegerOrInfinity) -> from\n  coerce end -> to\n  if this now detached → TypeError\n  copy [from,to) into new immutable buffer\n```\n\nGood, that matches.\n\ntransferToImmutable(newLength):\n- RequireInternalSlot; shared → TypeError; if newLength undefined → newByteLength = byteLength; else ToIndex(newLength).\n- if detached → TypeError (this-is-not-detachable)\n- if immutable → TypeError (this-is-not-detachable also checks immutable)\n- detach source, return immutable buffer.\n\nOrder per spec: RequireInternalSlot, IsShared, newByteLength computed (ToIndex), IsDetached → TypeError, IsImmutable → TypeError, detachKey check, copy, detach.\n\nLet me check new-length-coercion.js to make sure newLength coercion happens before detach check... Actually it might test that coercion of newLength is not performed if detached. this-is-not-detachable passes detached + immutable and both should throw regardless of args. Let me not over-worry; I'll coerce newLength then check detached/immutable — but this-is-not-detachable.js calls `fn.call(detached)` and `fn.call(immutable)` with no length arg, and `fn.call(immutable, 8)`. Let me check exact.\n\nLet me also check: immutable buffer passed to transferToImmutable must throw TypeError. Our WeakSet tracking handles that.\n\nNow the `.immutable` getter behavior for correct \"this\": it must throw TypeError for non-ArrayBuffer receivers. Test this-has-no-arraybufferdata-internal uses `Int8Array.prototype` prototype chains etc. Let me check that test fully. And this-is-sharedarraybuffer expects TypeError on SharedArrayBuffer. And `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(ArrayBuffer.prototype, \"immutable\").get` must exist and be a getter (prop-desc uses verifyPrimordialAccessorProperty).\n\nAlso `prop-desc.js` for each method uses verifiers checking name/length/descriptor. Let me check exact expected name/length values.\n\nLet me read the prop-desc files and this-has-no-arraybufferdata files fully.",
