t wait: tests like `this-is-not-object.js` call `ArrayBuffer.prototype.transferToImmutable` etc. — these are my polyfilled methods. Good.\n\nNow let me also consider `this-is-sharedarraybuffer.js`. It calls the getter/method with a SharedArrayBuffer receiver and expects TypeError. My `thisIsArrayBuffer` helper: check `this` is an object with ArrayBufferData internal slot and not SharedArrayBuffer. In JS: `this instanceof ArrayBuffer` — but SharedArrayBuffer is a different constructor, and `sab instanceof ArrayBuffer` is false. However, a plain object `{}` is also not instanceof ArrayBuffer → throw TypeError. And `new Int8Array(8)` — `ta instanceof ArrayBuffer`? No, typed arrays aren't instanceof ArrayBuffer. Their `.buffer` is, but the typed array itself isn't. Good, so `this instanceof ArrayBuffer` catches: non-arraybuffers throw; SharedArrayBuffer is not instanceof ArrayBuffer → throws. \n\nBut careful: what about a subclass instance `class My extends ArrayBuffer {}`? `new My(8) instanceof ArrayBuffer` true — should be valid (has internal slot). Fine.\n\nAlso `this-has-no-arraybufferdata-internal` receiver \"ArrayBuffer.prototype\" — `ArrayBuffer.prototype instanceof ArrayBuffer`? The prototype is an object, not instanceof ArrayBuffer → throws. Good. And \"TypedArray\" `new Int8Array(8)` false → throws. \"DataView\" false → throws. Plain object/array/function false → throws. \n\nNow let me also double check: `this.isSharedArrayBuffer` — detection. `this instanceof SharedArrayBuffer` returns false for SAB? Let me verify in Node: `new SharedArrayBuffer(4) instanceof SharedArrayBuffer` → true. And `new SharedArrayBuffer(4) instanceof ArrayBuffer` → false. Good. So `this instanceof ArrayBuffer` alone suffices to reject SAB. I don't even need shared checks. But to be safe I'll also explicitly exclude SAB.\n\nNow, the biggest question: Node's `ArrayBuffer.prototype.transfer` exists? Let me verify. And `structuredClone`. Let me test in node.\n\nLet me write a quick proto