            "text": "Node's `transfer` gives non-resizable result with maxByteLength == byteLength. \n\nNow, one subtle issue: `ab.transfer(8)` detaches ab AND returns transferred buffer. Good. But note `transfer` it's already non-resizable. So returned immutable buffer: byteLength correct, resizable:false, maxByteLength==byteLength. \n\nNow let me prototype the full polyfill in Node against the actual test files by running them. Let me build a quick test harness. Actually the cleanest is to directly run the actual test262 files in Node with the polyfill prepended, using a minimal test262 assert harness. But the repo has harness. Let me just prototype the polyfill functions and run a few test files manually with minimal stubs.\n\nActually, better approach: write the polyfill, then run the actual test files with Node using the real test262 includes (detachArrayBuffer.js etc.) via a small runner. Let me check if test262 provides standalone harness files (includes/) that I can load.\n\nFor running in Node directly I'd need `assert`, `compareArray`, `formatSimpleValue`, `isNegativeZero`, `$DETACHBUFFER`, `verifyPrimordialCallableProperty`, `verifyPrimordialAccessorProperty`. These are test262 harness includes. This is getting complicated to run standalone.\n\nBetter: just wire the polyfill into the crate (harness_e19_85.js + include_str + unit test + allowlist), then build and use the existing probe to test. But the skill wants red→green: write failing test first.\n\nLet me plan the \"red\" step: add a unit test in lib.rs `harness_e19_85_arraybuffer_immutable` that exercises the polyfilled behavior (transferToImmutable returns immutable, sliceToImmutable, .immutable getter, not-a-constructor, TypeErrors). This test will FAIL (red) before I add the polyfill include_str, and pass after.\n\nActually, since I need to add the polyfill file and include_str together, the red test and green change are intertwined. Let me follow: first write the test in lib.rs referencing behavi