      "output": "<path>/Users/jaredhembrow/Projects/draconic/draconic/ROADMAP.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Draconic Roadmap\n2: \n3: Source of truth for completeness, together with the test suite.  \n4: **Status**: `todo` | `in_progress` | `done` | `blocked`\n5: \n6: A item is `done` only when its tests are green on every applicable target (`js`, `native`, or both).\n7: \n8: **Platform capability goal.** Draconic targets systems + scripting + server **capability-class parity** with Rust, Go, and Node: host/process control, stdlib I/O and networking, concurrency, FFI, packaging, tooling, and shippable distribution—on top of full ECMAScript, TS-inspired types, and native dual-world codegen—not identical APIs, package counts, or platform monopolies. Completeness means a team can replace simple services and harden toward production without leaving the language for routine OS, net, crypto, and package work. Advanced niches (full browser engine, JVM/CLR, CUDA stack, kernel/UEFI, bit-identical Node/V8 or rustc) are **non-goals** unless explicitly filed later.\n9: \n10: ## Legend\n11: \n12: - **Targets**: `js` | `native` | `both` | `compiler` (toolchain-only, no program emit)\n13: - **Tests**: path(s) that must pass\n14: - **Native observations**: `Targets: native`/`both` means fixtures assert **program results** on native (`native.stdout` / equivalent), not the B08 LLVM hello-stub fallback (`hello\\n` only)\n15: - **Phase tracks**: historical **B / E / T / N / U** remain the language/toolchain spine. Platform tracks: **H** host I/O & networking, **K** packages, **F** FFI, **C** concurrency, **L** stdlib libs, **D** distribution, **R** reliability/security; product/spec **P** / **S**. Prefer draining open spine `todo`s when Loop intent is conformance; claim platform rows when building real programs.\n16: - **Locked decisions**: host sockets-first + HTTP helpers → ADR-0008; Go-style git packages → ADR-0009.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## B — Bootstrap (spine before full Conformance velocity)\n21: \n22: | ID | Status | Targets | Item | Tests |\n23: |----|--------|---------|------|-------|\n24: | B01 | done | compiler | Lexer: scan source into tokens (identifiers, keywords, punctuators, literals, EOF) | `crates/draconic-lexer` |\n25: | B02 | done | compiler | Parser + AST: parse a minimal Program; AST dump stable for snapshots | `crates/draconic-parser`, `crates/draconic-ast` |\n26: | B03 | done | compiler | CLI: `draconic parse <file>` prints AST dump | `crates/draconic-cli` |\n27: | B04 | done | compiler | Binder: scopes and symbol resolution for minimal Program | `crates/draconic-check` |\n28: | B05 | done | compiler | Checker: TypeScript-inspired types for minimal Program | `crates/draconic-check` |\n29: | B06 | done | compiler | Shared IR: lower minimal typed Program to IR | `crates/draconic-ir` |\n30: | B07 | done | js | JS backend: emit runnable JS for minimal Program | `crates/draconic-backend-js`, `tests/integration` |\n31: | B08 | done | native | LLVM backend stub + Runtime hello: native binary prints | `crates/draconic-backend-llvm`, `crates/draconic-runtime` |\n32: | B09 | done | native | GC hello: allocate string/object on native heap | `crates/draconic-runtime` |\n33: | B10 | done | both | CLI: `draconic build --target js\\|native` end-to-end | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n34: \n35: ---\n36: \n37: ## E — ECMA-262 Conformance (grow via Loop; cluster by area)\n38: \n39: Each cluster expands into finer rows as the Loop reaches it. Until then the cluster is the unit.\n40: \n41: | ID | Status | Targets | Item | Tests |\n42: |----|--------|---------|------|-------|\n43: | E00 | done | both | Conformance harness: load fixtures, run on js + native runners | `tests/conformance` |\n44: | E01 | done | js | Expressions & operators (ECMA-262 §12–13 core) | `tests/conformance/es/expressions` |\n45: | E01.01 | done | js | Numeric arithmetic: `+` `-` `*` `/` `%`, unary `+`/`-`, grouping/precedence | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n46: | E01.02 | done | js | Comparison & equality: `<` `<=` `>` `>=` `==` `!=` `===` `!==` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n47: | E01.03 | done | js | Logical: `&&` `\\|\\|` `!` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n48: | E01.04 | done | js | Remaining §12–13 (bitwise, assignment, conditional, update, `**`, comma, …) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n49: | E01.04.01 | done | js | Bitwise: `&` `\\|` `^` `~` `<<` `>>` `>>>` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n50: | E01.04.02 | done | js | Exponentiation: `**` (right-associative) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n51: | E01.04.03 | done | js | Conditional (ternary): `cond ? a : b` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n52: | E01.04.04 | done | js | Assignment: `=` (simple, right-associative) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n53: | E01.04.05 | done | js | Update: prefix/postfix `++` `--` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n54: | E01.04.06 | done | js | Comma operator: `,` (left-to-right, yields RHS) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n55: | E01.04.07 | done | js | Unary keywords: `typeof` `void` `delete` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n56: | E01.04.08 | done | js | Compound assignment: `+=` `-=` `*=` `/=` `%=` `**=` `<<=` `>>=` `>>>=` `&=` `^=` `\\|=` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n57: | E01.04.09 | done | js | Nullish coalescing `??` and logical assignment: `&&=` `\\|\\|=` `??=` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/expressions` |\n58: | E02 | done | js | Statements & control flow (§14) | `tests/conformance/es/statements` |\n59: | E02.01 | done | js | `if` / `else` (incl. block bodies) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n60: | E02.02 | done | js | `while` loops (incl. block bodies) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n61: | E02.03 | done | js | `do` / `while` loops (incl. block bodies) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n62: | E02.04 | done | js | `for` loops: `for (init; test; update)` (incl. `let` init, omitted clauses, block bodies) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n63: | E02.05 | done | js | `break` / `continue` (unlabeled, in loops) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n64: | E02.06 | done | js | `switch` / `case` / `default` (incl. fall-through, `break`) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n65: | E02.07 | done | js | Labeled statements + labeled `break` / `continue` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n66: | E02.08 | done | js | `for-in` / `for-of` loops (incl. `let` binding, block bodies; iterate strings) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n67: | E02.09 | done | js | `const` declarations (required initializer; no reassignment; `for`/`for-of`/`for-in` binding) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/statements` |\n68: | E03 | done | js | Functions, closures, arguments, arrows (§15) | `tests/conformance/es/functions` |\n69: | E03.01 | done | js | Function declaration + `return` + call (no params) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/functions` |\n70: | E03.02 | done | js | Function parameters + call with arguments | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/functions` |\n71: | E03.03 | done | js | Nested function declarations + free-variable capture (outer `let`/params) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/functions` |\n72: | E03.04 | done | js | Function expressions: `function (params) { … }` as values (incl. named, IIFE) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/functions` |\n73: | E03.05 | done | js | Arrow functions: `(params) => expr` and `(params) => { … }` (simple ident params; no `this`) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/functions` |\n74: | E03.06 | done | js | Default parameters: `function f(a = expr)` / `(a = expr) => …` (missing/`undefined` → default) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/functions` |\n75: | E03.07 | done | js | Rest parameters: `function f(...args)` / `(...args) => …` (last param; binds array of remaining args) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/functions` |\n76: | E04 | done | js | Objects, prototypes, `this`, property access (§10, §20) | `tests/conformance/es/objects` |\n77: | E04.01 | done | js | Object literals `{ k: v }` + property access `obj.k` / `obj[\"k\"]` (read; string keys) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/objects` |\n78: | E04.02 | done | js | Property assignment: `obj.k = v` / `obj[\"k\"] = v` (simple `=`; read-back) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/objects` |\n79: | E04.03 | done | js | `this` + method call: `obj.m()` / `obj[\"m\"]()` preserves `this`; `function` methods as values | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/objects` |\n80: | E04.04 | done | js | `new` constructor: `new F(args)` with `function` ctor setting `this` props; returns instance | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/objects` |\n81: | E04.05 | done | js | Prototypes: `F.prototype.m = function…`; instances inherit methods; `this` in prototype methods | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/objects` |\n82: | E04.06 | done | js | Object literal sugar: property shorthand `{ a }`, method shorthand `{ m() {…} }`, computed keys `{ [expr]: v }` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/objects` |\n83: | E05 | done | js | Classes (§15.7) | `tests/conformance/es/classes` |\n84: | E05.01 | done | js | Class declaration: `class C { constructor(…) {…} m(…) {…} }`; `new C(args)`; instance methods + `this` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/classes` |\n85: | E05.02 | done | js | Class heritage: `extends Parent`; `super(…)` in constructor; inherit parent prototype methods | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/classes` |\n86: | E05.03 | done | js | Static methods: `static m(…) {…}`; call as `C.m(…)` / `new C().constructor.m` not required; no `this` instance binding | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/classes` |\n87: | E05.04 | done | js | `super` property access: `super.m(…)` / `super.prop` in methods (parent prototype, correct `this`) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/classes` |\n88: | E06 | done | js | Arrays, iterators, spread/rest | `tests/conformance/es/arrays` |\n89: | E06.01 | done | js | Array literals `[a, b]` + index access `arr[i]` / `arr.length` (read) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/arrays` |\n90: | E06.02 | done | js | Array element assignment: `arr[i] = v` (simple `=`; read-back; length may grow) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/arrays` |\n91: | E06.03 | done | js | Spread in array literals: `[...a]` / `[...a, b]` / `[a, ...b, c]` (iterable copy/concat) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/arrays` |\n92: | E06.04 | done | js | Spread in call/new args: `f(...a)` / `f(x, ...a, y)` / `new F(...a)` (iterable expand into arguments) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/arrays` |\n93: | E06.05 | done | js | `for-of` over arrays: iterate elements; `let`/assign binding; block bodies; nested arrays | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/arrays` |\n94: | E06.06 | done | js | Array destructuring: `let [a, b] = arr` / `let [a, ...rest] = arr` / assignment `[a, b] = arr` (holes, defaults deferred) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/arrays` |\n95: | E07 | done | js | Strings, template literals, UTF-16 semantics | `tests/conformance/es/strings` |\n96: | E07.01 | done | js | String literals (`\"`/`'`) + concat `+` + `.length` + index `s[i]` (read; basic escapes `\\n` `\\r` `\\t` `\\\\` `\\'` `\\\"` `\\0`) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/strings` |\n97: | E07.02 | done | js | Template literals: `` `…` `` / `` `a${x}b` `` (untagged; cooked escapes; multi-interp) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/strings` |\n98: | E07.03 | done | js | Unicode escapes: `\\xHH`, `\\uXXXX`, `\\u{X…}` in string/template literals (cooked; well-formed scalar values) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/strings` |\n99: | E07.04 | done | js | Tagged templates: `tag\\`…\\`` / `tag\\`a${x}b\\`` (tag call; cooked quasis + interpolations as args) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `es/strings` |\n100: | E07.05 | done | js | UTF-16 code-unit semantics: `.length`/index