    "type": "text",
    "text": "## Objective\n- Run the draconic-loop skill exactly once: claim the next ROADMAP.md `todo` item (E19.86 module namespace internals residual), implement it test-first, mark it `done` only when `cargo test --workspace` is green, then stop without starting a second item.\n\n## Important Details\n- Skill steps: Claim → Orient → Red → Green → Verify. Empty-todo guard: if no `todo` row exists anywhere, stop immediately.\n- Exactly one `in_progress` row at a time. Verify = probe newly allowlisted paths via `cargo build -p draconic-test262 --bin probe --release` + `./target/release/probe` (paths on stdin), then `cargo test` (touched crates), then `cargo test --workspace`.\n- Repo: branch `main`, HEAD=`824f408` (E19.85); uncommitted local edit to `tests/test262/src/bin/probe.rs` (removed 160-char message truncation, kept as debug aid); untracked `.loop/logs/`.\n- E19.86 row found in ROADMAP.md (line 311 area): `in_progress | js | Module namespace internals residual: [[Get]]/[[Set]]/[[HasProperty]] / export-name string bindings | crates/draconic-linker` / backend-js, `tests/test262`.\n- Design validated with a Node v26 prototype (`/tmp/prox_verify.mjs`): Proxy-based namespace polyfill matches native semantics — `Object.keys(ns)` / `for-in` / `hasOwnProperty` on an uninit binding throw ReferenceError; `Object.getOwnPropertyNames`/`Reflect.ownKeys` don't throw; ownKeys sorted with Symbol.toStringTag last; getters invoked through proxy traps.\n- Node v26 native `super.foo = 14` on a namespace receiver throws **TypeError**, but `super-access-to-tdz-binding.js` asserts **ReferenceError** — harness polyfill must implement spec behavior (GetOwnProperty→Get→TDZ), not rely on Node's native exotic namespace.\n- Baseline: suite present at `third_party/test262`, baseline-report pass=43512 fail=0.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Claimed E19.86 in ROADMAP.md: marked `in_progress`.\n- All non-FIXTURE `test/language/module-code/namespace/internals/*.js` were already allowlisted; the 8 previously allowlisted paths all passed.\n- Ran full internals-dir probe with newly built release probe: **19 PASS**, several FAIL (define-own-property, delete-exported-init, delete-exported-uninit, get-nested-namespace-dflt-skip, get-nested-namespace-props-nrml, plus truncated tail).\n- Read all relevant fixtures: delete-{exported-init,exported-uninit,non-exported}, define-own-property, get-own-property-{str-found-init,str-found-uninit,str-not-found,sym}, set, is-extensible, prevent-extensions, get-prototype-of, set-prototype-of-null, own-property-keys-binding-types, super-access-to-tdz-binding.\n- Implemented the eager namespace rework in `crates/draconic-linker/src/lib.rs`:\n  - Replaced `shared_ns_by_id` (plain object literal, post-body emit) with `shared_ns_setup: Vec<(usize, Stmt)>` emitted **before any module body**.\n  - New `shared_namespace_helper_stmts()` builds the `__draconic_make_ns(pairs, exportNames, toStringTag)` Proxy helper (null proto target, sorted non-configurable keys, traps: get/has/getOwnPropertyDescriptor/ownKeys/defineProperty/deleteProperty/set/getPrototypeOf/setPrototypeOf/isExtensible/preventExtensions; `get` returns `getters[p]()` so TDZ ReferenceError propagates lazily).\n  - New `make_shared_namespace_binding(local, resolved, mangled, span)` generates `let __ns{id} = __draconic_make_ns([[\"name\", function () { return <final>; }], ...], [...], \"Module\");`.\n  - Removed the post-body emit block and the now-unused `namespace_object_props_resolved`.\n- `cargo build -p draconic-linker` clean (no warnings); `cargo run -p draconic-cli -- build --target js` on a fixture emits helpers + `let __ns0/1/2`.\n- Root cause of remaining failures identified: emitted output (e.g. `/tmp/nsdbg/out.mjs`) contains **duplicate `let __ns0` declarations** — the three namespaces from `get-nested-namespace-props-nrml-{1,2,3}_FIXTURE` all emit as `__ns0` even though linker's debug shows correct `__ns0/__ns1/__ns2`. The renaming happens **after** the linker, downstream in `draconic-ir` lowering: `DEBUG IR locals: [(56, \"__ns0\"), (57, \"__ns1\"), (58, \"__ns2\")]` is correct at check/lower entry.\n- Removed temporary `eprintln!` debug lines from linker (the two `DEBUG ns target`/`DEBUG src` patches) and from `crates/draconic-ir/src/lib.rs` (the `DEBUG IR locals` patch in `lower()`).\n\n### Active\n- Cause of the `__ns1`→`__ns0` / `__ns2`→`__ns0` rename in the emitted JS is **not yet located**. Binder symbols are correct (3 distinct names), so the collision likely comes from:\n  - `bind_unique_local`/symbol-reuse logic in `crates/draconic-check` or\n  - the linked Program being **re-bind/re-symboled** before `lower()` (the `check_path` pipeline parses the linked program's synthetic `let` stmts and may collapse/reuse identifiers), or\n  - `crates/draconic-ir` `lower()`'s `locals`/`body` handling.\n- Debug artifacts in `/tmp/nsdbg/` (out.mjs, out2..out5.mjs, FIXTURE copies) still present for reproducing the failure.\n- `tests/test262/src/bin/probe.rs` still has the uncommitted truncation-removal edit (intentional debug aid).\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Trace where `__ns1`/`__ns2` get renamed to `__ns0` between linker output (correct) and emitted JS: inspect `draconic-check` `bind_*`/symbol-reuse logic (note binder comment \"unique id\" and stale-symbol handling around lines 883–1311 of `crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs`), and confirm whether the linked program is re-bound after `link_entry` (e.g. in `check_path`/`compile_path` pipeline).\n2. Fix the naming collision so `__ns0/__ns1/__ns2` survive to emit directly (or allocate a distinct synthetic namespace local id at bind time).\n3. Re-probe `test/language/module-code/namespace/internals/*.js` (expect all green), add none (all 39 already allowlisted) or update allowlist if any path still fails, then run `cargo test --workspace`, mark E19.86 `done` in ROADMAP.md, regenerate baseline-report, and commit.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `ROADMAP.md` — E19.86 row marked `in_progress` (line 311 area).\n- `crates/draconic-linker/src/lib.rs` — new/changed: `shared_ns_setup` build (~line 459), up-front emit block (~line 500), `shared_namespace_helper_stmts` (new, ~line 2280), `make_shared_namespace_binding` (new, ~line 2477), removed `namespace_object_props_resolved`; existing: `shared_namespace_binding_name`/`deferred_namespace_binding_name` (1369/1373), `collect_resolved_exports` (686), `final_binding_name` (1377), `link_entry` (24).\n- `crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs` — binder/symbol-reuse logic to inspect for the rename.\n- `crates/draconic-ir/src/lib.rs` — `lower()` (line 546) locals construction; `DEBUG IR locals` confirmed names are correct here.\n- `crates/draconic-frontend/src/lib.rs` — `compile_path` (38) → `check_path` → `lower`; possible re-bind of the linked program.\n- `crates/draconic-backend-js/src/lib.rs` / `src/emit.rs` — emitter uses `names: HashMap<LocalId, &str>` from `module.locals`; `local_name` (emit.rs 1277).\n- `/tmp/nsdbg/` — repro files: `get-nested-namespace-props-nrml.js` + 3 FIXTURE copies, `out.mjs` showing `let __ns0` ×3.\n- `tests/test262/src/bin/probe.rs` — stdin probe (locally modified).\n- `tests/test262/src/lib.rs` — runner; `tests/test262/allowlist.txt` / `baseline-report.md`.",
