      "output": "<path>/Users/jaredhembrow/Projects/draconic/draconic/.loop/logs/loop-20260806-044227.log</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: sleep between loops: 0s (set with SLEEP=<seconds>)\n2: stall watchdog: 900s idle → kill (continue) (STALL_SEC / STALL_ACTION)\n3: prompt: Run the draconic-loop skill exactly once: claim the next ROADMAP.md item, implement it test-first, mark it done only when cargo test --workspace is green, then stop. Do not start a second item.\n4: \n5: ===== loop 1/100 =====\n6: {\n7:   \"type\": \"step_start\",\n8:   \"timestamp\": 1785955351259,\n9:   \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n10:   \"part\": {\n11:     \"id\": \"prt_fd33bfad90012iR1IloGtD2XJr\",\n12:     \"messageID\": \"msg_fd33befdd001qMg6MmQAAzg74s\",\n13:     \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n14:     \"snapshot\": \"b3c4ba573779ddf37149459ec2e2c41f57f1ba1c\",\n15:     \"type\": \"step-start\"\n16:   }\n17: }\n18: {\n19:   \"type\": \"tool_use\",\n20:   \"timestamp\": 1785955352482,\n21:   \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n22:   \"part\": {\n23:     \"type\": \"tool\",\n24:     \"tool\": \"skill\",\n25:     \"callID\": \"call_00_N8XOAiIaulKoQX8Qdq6Y2491\",\n26:     \"state\": {\n27:       \"status\": \"completed\",\n28:       \"input\": {\n29:         \"name\": \"draconic-loop\"\n30:       },\n31:       \"output\": \"<skill_content name=\\\"draconic-loop\\\">\\n# Skill: draconic-loop\\n\\n# Draconic Loop\\n\\nOne **Loop** = one atomic Roadmap item, red → green → done. Completeness is **Roadmap + Conformance suite**, not model judgment.\\n\\nRead before work: `CONTEXT.md`, relevant `docs/adr/`, `ROADMAP.md`.\\n\\n## Steps\\n\\n1. **Claim** — In `ROADMAP.md`, find the first `todo` item whose blockers are satisfied (lower bootstrap IDs done; do not start `E*` clusters until **B10** is `done` unless the user overrides). Prefer historical **B/E/T/N/U** before Phase 2 **P/S** unless the user asks for product/spec work. Set it to `in_progress`. Exactly one `in_progress` at a time.\\n   - **Empty-todo guard:** if there is **no** `todo` row anywhere on the Roadmap, **stop immediately**. Do not invent work, do not add speculative Roadmap rows, do not “keep the loop busy.” Report empty board; further work needs a human or a vault issue.\\n2. **Orient** — Read existing tests and code for that item’s **Tests** paths. Skim ADRs if the item touches IR, Runtime, Embed, or dual worlds.\\n3. **Red** — Add or extend tests that fail for the missing behavior. Prefer crate unit tests for compiler pieces; `tests/conformance/**` for language semantics; both backends when **Targets** is `both`.\\n4. **Green** — Implement the minimum to pass. No silent subsetting of ECMA-262: if the item’s scope is large, **split** the Roadmap row into child IDs (e.g. `E01.01`) and complete only the claimed child this Loop.\\n5. **Verify** — Run `cargo test` for touched crates, then `cargo test --workspace` (**fast by default**). Full Test262 allowlist (~37k Node runs) is **opt-in**:\\n   - Default: workspace tests use a **smoke** allowlist slice only (`DRACONIC_TEST262_FULL` unset).\\n   - Always **probe** newly added allowlist paths (or the item’s target fixtures) with `cargo build -p draconic-test262 --bin probe --release` + `./target/release/probe` before `done`.\\n   - For **Expand allowlist** rows or when you changed man... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n32:       \"metadata\": {\n33:         \"name\": \"draconic-loop\",\n34:         \"dir\": \"/Users/jaredhembrow/Projects/draconic/draconic/.agents/skills/draconic-loop\",\n35:         \"truncated\": false\n36:       },\n37:       \"title\": \"Loaded skill: draconic-loop\",\n38:       \"time\": {\n39:         \"start\": 1785955352470,\n40:         \"end\": 1785955352481\n41:       }\n42:     },\n43:     \"id\": \"prt_fd33bff41001ptuB5UalQedblH\",\n44:     \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n45:     \"messageID\": \"msg_fd33befdd001qMg6MmQAAzg74s\"\n46:   }\n47: }\n48: {\n49:   \"type\": \"step_finish\",\n50:   \"timestamp\": 1785955352622,\n51:   \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n52:   \"part\": {\n53:     \"id\": \"prt_fd33c002c0015TyNYcw1BZtCOz\",\n54:     \"reason\": \"tool-calls\",\n55:     \"snapshot\": \"e5d03f6849511cf07a7cc3d5fe7715add09656a4\",\n56:     \"messageID\": \"msg_fd33befdd001qMg6MmQAAzg74s\",\n57:     \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n58:     \"type\": \"step-finish\",\n59:     \"tokens\": {\n60:       \"total\": 20015,\n61:       \"input\": 19950,\n62:       \"output\": 46,\n63:       \"reasoning\": 19,\n64:       \"cache\": {\n65:         \"write\": 0,\n66:         \"read\": 0\n67:       }\n68:     },\n69:     \"cost\": 0\n70:   }\n71: }\n72: {\n73:   \"type\": \"step_start\",\n74:   \"timestamp\": 1785955353908,\n75:   \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n76:   \"part\": {\n77:     \"id\": \"prt_fd33c0532001EKeqjMwbO9dz97\",\n78:     \"messageID\": \"msg_fd33c007b001vvjfv00nGz9kki\",\n79:     \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n80:     \"snapshot\": \"d9b986e4c3549110e4dc19d8c06342acd05b879e\",\n81:     \"type\": \"step-start\"\n82:   }\n83: }\n84: {\n85:   \"type\": \"tool_use\",\n86:   \"timestamp\": 1785955354669,\n87:   \"sessionID\": \"ses_02cc41160ffehCjhAA5qw70dvg\",\n88:   \"part\": {\n89:     \"type\": \"tool\",\n90:     \"tool\": \"read\",\n91:     \"callID\": \"call_00_l8iqodj71mrzDjXojYiR4444\",\n92:     \"state\": {\n93:       \"status\": \"completed\",\n94:       \"input\": {\n95:         \"filePath\": \"/Users/jaredhembrow/Projects/draconic/draconic/ROADMAP.md\"\n96:       },\n97:       \"output\": \"<path>/Users/jaredhembrow/Projects/draconic/draconic/ROADMAP.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Draconic Roadmap\\n2: \\n3: Source of truth for completeness, together with the test suite.  \\n4: **Status**: `todo` | `in_progress` | `done` | `blocked`\\n5: \\n6: A item is `done` only when its tests are green on every applicable target (`js`, `native`, or both).\\n7: \\n8: **Platform capability goal.** Draconic targets systems + scripting + server **capability-class parity** with Rust, Go, and Node: host/process control, stdlib I/O and networking, concurrency, FFI, packaging, tooling, and shippable distribution—on top of full ECMAScript, TS-inspired types, and native dual-world codegen—not identical APIs, package counts, or platform monopolies. Completeness means a team can replace simple services and harden toward production without leaving the language for routine OS, net, crypto, and package work. Advanced niches (full browser engine, JVM/CLR, CUDA stack, kernel/UEFI, bit-identical Node/V8 or rustc) are **non-goals** unless explicitly filed later.\\n9: \\n10: ## Legend\\n11: \\n12: - **Targets**: `js` | `native` | `both` | `compiler` (toolchain-only, no program emit)\\n13: - **Tests**: path(s) that must pass\\n14: - **Native observations**: `Targets: native`/`both` means fixtures assert **program results** on native (`native.stdout` / equivalent), not the B08 LLVM hello-stub fallback (`hello\\\\n` only)\\n15: - **Phase tracks**: historical **B / E / T / N / U** remain the language/toolchain spine. Platform tracks: **H** host I/O & networking, **K** packages, **F** FFI, **C** concurrency, **L** stdlib libs, **D** distribution, **R** reliability/security; product/spec **P** / **S**. Prefer draining open spine `todo`s when Loop intent is conformance; claim platform rows when building real programs.\\n16: - **Locked decisions**: host sockets-first + HTTP helpers → ADR-0008; Go-style git packages → ADR-0009.\\n17: \\n18: ---\\n19: \\n20: ## B — Bootstrap (spine b... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n98:       \"metadata\": {\n99:         \"preview\": \"# Draconic Roadmap\\n\\nSource of truth for completeness, together with the test suite.  \\n**Status**: `todo` | `in_progress` | `done` | `blocked`\\n\\nA item is `done` only when its tests are green on every applicable target (`js`, `native`, or both).\\n\\n**Platform capability goal.** Draconic targets systems + scripting + server **capability-class parity** with Rust, Go, and Node: host/process control, stdlib I/O and networking, concurrency, FFI, packaging, tooling, and shippable distribution—on top of full ECMAScript, TS-inspired types, and native dual-world codegen—not identical APIs, package counts, or platform monopolies. Completeness means a team can replace simple services and harden toward production without leaving the language for routine OS, net, crypto, and package work. Advanced niches (full browser engine, JVM/CLR, CUDA stack, kernel/UEFI, bit-identical Node/V8 or rustc) are **non-goals** unless explicitly filed later.\\n\\n## Legend\\n\\n- **Targets**: `js` | `native` | `both` | `compiler` (toolchain-only, no program emit)\\n- **Tests**: path(s) that must pass\\n- **Native observations**: `Targets: native`/`both` means fixtures assert **program results** on native (`native.stdout` / equivalent), not the B08 LLVM hello-stub fallback (`hello\\\\n` only)\\n- **Phase tracks**: historical **B / E / T / N / U** remain the language/toolchain spine. Platform tracks: **H** host I/O & networking, **K** packages, **F** FFI, **C** concurrency, **L** stdlib libs, **D** distribution, **R** reliability/security; product/spec **P** / **S**. Prefer draining open spine `todo`s when Loop intent is conformance; claim platform rows when building real programs.\\n- **Locked decisions**: host sockets-first + HTTP helpers → ADR-0008; Go-style git packages → ADR-0009.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## B — Bootstrap (spine before full Conformance velocity)\",\n100:         \"truncated\": true,\n101:         \"loaded\": [],\n102:         \"display\": {\n103:           \"type\": \"file\",\n104:           \"path\": \"/Users/jaredhembrow/Projects/draconic/draconic/ROADMAP.md\",\n105:           \"text\": \"# Draconic Roadmap\\n\\nSource of truth for completeness, together with the test suite.  \\n**Status**