      "output": "---\nid: issues-18\ncreated_at: \"2026-07-29\"\nupdated_at: \"2026-08-01\"\narea: planning\ndomain: language\ntitle: \"Complete Roadmap seed data\"\ndescription: \"Finish seeding platform tracks so every claimed capability is Loop-atomic with Tests paths, critical paths, and no half-seeded clusters.\"\nstatus: closed\nissue-type: feature-request\nseverity: medium\ntags:\n  - planning\n  - issue\n  - enhancement\n  - closed\n  - roadmap\n  - seed\n---\n\n# Complete Roadmap seed data\n\n## Description\n\nFinish the Roadmap **seed data** so platform capability tracks are fully seeded the way **H** and **K** already are: Loop-sized `todo` rows, concrete **Tests** paths, parent/child structure where clusters are too large for one Loop, and critical-path notes where a success demo depends on order.\n\n**H** (ADR-0008 / [[issues-16-roadmap-e2e-http-server]]) and **K** (ADR-0009 / [[issues-17-roadmap-git-package-manager]]) were seeded with deep children + v1 done bars. **F / C / L / D / R** (and light **P / S** extras) still look like first-pass parent seeds — often one row per cluster, uneven child depth, no critical-path / v1-done notes. Completing seed data means closing that gap **without inventing new product directions**.\n\n## Affected\n\n- `ROADMAP.md` — sections **F**, **C**, **L**, **D**, **R**; review **P** / **S** / residual **N** / **U** for incomplete seeds only\n- Legend / “How the Loop updates” if seed policy needs one line of clarity\n- Optional ADRs only if a seed pass surfaces a locked decision that is not already ADR-0008/0009\n\n## Observed\n\n| Track | Seed state today |\n|-------|------------------|\n| **H** | Deep children H00–H17 + critical path to http-echo |\n| **K** | Deep children K01–K11 + v1 done bar |\n| **F** | F01–F09 parent-level only |\n| **C** | C01–C06 parent-level only |\n| **L** | L01–L10 parent-level only |\n| **D** | D01–D05 parent-level only |\n| **R** | R01–R06 parent-level only |\n| **P / S** | Light Phase 2 seeds (P01–P02 / S01 done); P03–P05 / S02 present |\n\nSpine **B/E/T/N/U** honesty already handled by [[issues-1-roadmap-honesty-pass]] and related closes — out of scope unless a seed audit finds a missing *seed* (not implementation).\n\n## Impact\n\n- Loop claims coarse parents and either under-delivers or balloons one session.\n- Critical-path work (e.g. FFI → real systems demos, install path for distribution) has no ordered bar like H→http-echo or K→temp-git e2e.\n- Half-seeded tracks invite ad-hoc invention when the board looks “thin” on a track despite parent rows existing.\n\n## Proposed Fix\n\n1. **Audit** F/C/L/D/R (and P/S/N residual) against H/K quality bar:\n   - Each row = one Loop (or split to `X.NN` children).\n   - **Targets** + **Tests** path real or clearly “create on implement”.\n---ISSUES OPEN---\nissues-1-roadmap-honesty-pass.md\nissues-10-collapse-llvm-multipath.md\nissues-11-linker-own-module.md\nissues-12-split-mega-files-seams.md\nissues-13-checker-target-neutral.md\nissues-14-unify-eval-embed-fold.md\nissues-15-deepen-ir-backend-diverge.md\nissues-16-roadmap-e2e-http-server.md\nissues-17-roadmap-git-package-manager.md\nissues-18-complete-roadmap-seed-data.md\ndocs/planning\ndocs/planning/out-of-scope\ndocs/planning/tasks\ndocs/planning/tasks/completed\ndocs/planning/plans\ndocs/planning/plans/completed\ndocs/planning/issues\ndocs/planning/issues/closed\n",
      "metadata": {
        "output": "---\nid: issues-18\ncreated_at: \"2026-07-29\"\nupdated_at: \"2026-08-01\"\narea: planning\ndomain: language\ntitle: \"Complete Roadmap seed data\"\ndescription: \"Finish seeding platform tracks so every claimed capability is Loop-atomic with Tests paths, critical paths, and no half-seeded clusters.\"\nstatus: closed\nissue-type: feature-request\nseverity: medium\ntags:\n  - planning\n  - issue\n  - enhancement\n  - closed\n  - roadmap\n  - seed\n---\n\n# Complete Roadmap seed data\n\n## Description\n\nFinish the Roadmap **seed data** so platform capability tracks are fully seeded the way **H** and **K** already are: Loop-sized `todo` rows, concrete **Tests** paths, parent/child structure where clusters are too large for one Loop, and critical-path notes where a success demo depends on order.\n\n**H** (ADR-0008 / [[issues-16-roadmap-e2e-http-server]]) and **K** (ADR-0009 / [[issues-17-roadmap-git-package-manager]]) were seeded with deep children + v1 done bars. **F / C / L / D / R** (and light **P / S** extras) still look like first-pass parent seeds — often one row per cluster, uneven child depth, no critical-path / v1-done notes. Completing seed data means closing that gap **without inventing new product directions**.\n\n## Affected\n\n- `ROADMAP.md` — sections **F**, **C**, **L**, **D**, **R**; review **P** / **S** / residual **N** / **U** for incomplete seeds only\n- Legend / “How the Loop updates” if seed policy needs one line of clarity\n- Optional ADRs only if a seed pass surfaces a locked decision that is not already ADR-0008/0009\n\n## Observed\n\n| Track | Seed state today |\n|-------|------------------|\n| **H** | Deep children H00–H17 + critical path to http-echo |\n| **K** | Deep children K01–K11 + v1 done bar |\n| **F** | F01–F09 parent-level only |\n| **C** | C01–C06 parent-level only |\n| **L** | L01–L10 parent-level only |\n| **D** | D01–D05 parent-level only |\n| **R** | R01–R06 parent-level only |\n| **P / S** | Light Phase 2 seeds (P01–P02 / S01 done); P03–P05 / S02 present |\n\nSpine **B/E/T/N/U** honesty already handled by [[issues-1-roadmap-honesty-pass]] and related closes — out of scope unless a seed audit finds a missing *seed* (not implementation).\n\n## Impact\n\n- Loop claims coarse parents and either under-delivers or balloons one session.\n- Critical-path work (e.g. FFI → real systems demos, install path for distribution) has no ordered bar like H→http-echo or K→temp-git e2e.\n- Half-seeded tracks invite ad-hoc invention when the board looks “thin” on a track despite parent rows existing.\n\n## Proposed Fix\n\n1. **Audit** F/C/L/D/R (and P/S/N residual) against H/K quality bar:\n   - Each row = one Loop (or split to `X.NN` children).\n   - **Targets** + **Tests** path real or clearly “create on implement”.\n---ISSUES OPEN---\nissues-1-roadmap-honesty-pass.md\nissues-10-collapse-llvm-multipath.md\nissues-11-linker-own-module.md\nissues-12-split-mega-files-seams.md\nissues-13-checker-target-neutral.md\nissues-14-unify-eval-embed-fold.md\nissues-15-deepen-ir-backend-diverge.md\nissues-16-roadmap-e2e-http-server.md\nissues-17-roadmap-git-package-manager.md\nissues-18-complete-roadmap-seed-data.md\ndocs/planning\ndocs/planning/out-of-scope\ndocs/planning/tasks\ndocs/planning/tasks/completed\ndocs/planning/plans\ndocs/planning/plans/completed\ndocs/planning/issues\ndocs/planning/issues/closed\n",
