    "text": "## Objective\n- Run the `draconic-loop` skill exactly once: claim the next `ROADMAP.md` `todo` item, implement test-first, mark `done` only when `cargo test --workspace` is green, then stop.\n\n## Important Details\n- Claimed item: **E19.87** — `Expand allowlist further after E19.82–E19.86 (next failure clusters from baseline probe)` — Targets `js`, Tests `tests/test262` (allowlist + baseline-report).\n- ROADMAP row was flipped to `in_progress`; must be flipped back to `done` before commit, then stop (one Loop only).\n- Branch `main`, HEAD `8523f0f`. `.loop/logs/` is untracked; working tree otherwise clean.\n- Suite: `third_party/test262` (53,716 JS files). Allowlist: `tests/test262/allowlist.txt` (45,494 entries). Baseline (`tests/test262/baseline-report.md`, git-ignored via `.gitignore:18`): `pass=43052 fail=2442`.\n- Workspace default = smoke only (first 32 allowlist entries). Full gate = `DRACONIC_TEST262_FULL` env var. Probe binary: `cargo build -p draconic-test262 --bin probe --release`, paths on stdin → PASS/FAIL lines.\n- **Root cause diagnosed**: commit `ebbd2ec` (E19.82) added `with_use_strict()` in `crates/draconic-ir/src/lib.rs:2158` which injects `Stmt::Expr(\"use strict\")` into every class ctor/method/accessor/static-block body (call sites ~3102, 3150, 3211, 3339, 3396, 3595, 3938). When a function has a non-simple parameter list (default/rest/destructured), the emitted JS is a Node SyntaxError: `Illegal 'use strict' directive in function with non-simple parameter list`.\n- Probe confirmed both `test/language/expressions/class/async-gen-method-static/dflt-params-arg-val-undefined.js` and the `statements/class` variant fail with that exact error.\n- Failure clusters are large: `language/(expressions|statements)/class/dstr` = 1,044+1,044 failing; plus 8 method kinds ×7, ×2 (expr/statement), and more (scope-*, params-dflt-*, static-init-*) — ~2,200+ class failures.\n- Node v26.0.0 verified: a non-simple-param method inside a strict IIFE works (strictness inherited from enclosing strict function), so strictness can move to the class-builder IIFE.\n- IR types: `Param { pattern: Pattern, default: Option<Expr>, rest: bool }` at `crates/draconic-ir/src/lib.rs:506`; `Pattern` at :490 (`Local` = simple; default/rest/Array/Object = non-simple).\n- Plan: add `\"use strict\"` directive to the class-builder IIFE body in `wrap_class_builder_iife` (line 1174, always empty params → legal), and skip the per-function directive when params are non-simple (strictness inherited).\n- `cargo build -p draconic-test262 --bin probe --release` already built successfully.\n- User instruction: exactly one item, test-first, `cargo test --workspace` green, then stop. Skill also requires probing newly added allowlist paths and the full `DRACONIC_TEST262_FULL` gate for Expand-allowlist rows.\n- `CONTEXT.md` and ADR 0007 (Test262 staged harness) have not yet been read — required by skill before implementation.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Read `ROADMAP.md`; claimed **E19.87** → `in_progress`.\n- Diagnosed the E19.82 `with_use_strict` codegen regression as the dominant allowlist-expansion failure cluster.\n- Confirmed failing paths via `./target/release/probe`.\n- Created test-first fixture `tests/conformance/fixtures/es/classes/class_non_simple_params.drac` covering: instance method default param + detached-`this`-is-undefined strict check; static generator default + rest; ctor default + destructured defaults; setter destructured param; static async method default param (asserts throw inside `.then` → Node v26 default unhandled-rejection=throw exits nonzero on failure).\n\n### Active\n- Todo list: claim + diagnose = completed; **Red**: confirm failing test / gate red = in progress; fix IR, green/probe/allowlist/full-gate, workspace verify, close+commit = pending.\n- Fixture `.meta` sidecar (`class_non_simple_params.meta`) **not yet written** — needs `id: es/classes/class_non_simple_params`, `targets: js`, `js.exit: 0`.\n\n### Blocked\n- None.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write `tests/conformance/fixtures/es/classes/class_non_simple_params.meta` (`id`, `targets: js`, `js.exit: 0`) and run the fixture via the conformance crate to confirm it is **red** (Node SyntaxError from the `\"use strict\"` directive).\n2. Read `CONTEXT.md` + ADR 0007 (skill requirement); then implement the IR fix: add `\"use strict\"` directive to the class-builder IIFE body in `wrap_class_builder_iife` (line 1174) and make `with_use_strict` skip the directive when the lowered param list is non-simple (call sites that have params: 3102, 3150, 3211, 3339, 3396 — safe: 3595 static block, 3938 field-init home method).\n3. Re-run fixture (green), add `crates/draconic-ir` unit test(s) for non-simple-param method/ctor/accessor lowering emitting no directive inside the non-simple list while class code stays strict.\n4. Probe the failing class clusters (start with `dstr` + method/accessor/generator paths from `tests/test262/baseline-report.md`), move newly-passing paths into `allowlist.txt`, regenerate `baseline-report.md`.\n5. Run `cargo test --workspace` (smoke default), then full gate `DRACONIC_TEST262_FULL=1 cargo test -p draconic-test262` (fail=0 required) plus probe newly added entries.\n6. Flip E19.87 to `done`, commit, stop — do not claim a second item.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `ROADMAP.md` — E19.87 row currently `in_progress`; must become `done`.\n- `crates/draconic-ir/src/lib.rs` — `with_use_strict` def :2158, call sites :3102/:3150/:3211/:3339/:3396/:3595/:3938; `wrap_class_builder_iife` :1174; `Param`/`Pattern` :490–510; `lower_class_local` :2606; `lower_class` :1045; `lower_class_expression` :1097.\n- `tests/test262/src/lib.rs` — harness; `default_run_does_not_fail_ci_without_suite` ~:3449 (smoke=first 32); `run_case` :1965; `run_case_inner` :1979; `allowlist_path()`; `write_baseline_report`.\n- `tests/test262/src/bin/probe.rs` — stdin path → PASS/FAIL; usage `./target/release/probe < paths.txt`.\n- `tests/test262/allowlist.txt` — 45,494 entries, source of truth for test262 conformance roll-in.\n- `tests/test262/baseline-report.md` — git-ignored generated report; failure clusters enumerated here.\n- `tests/conformance/fixtures/es/classes/class_non_simple_params.drac` — new red fixture (meta pending).\n- `tests/conformance/fixtures/es/classes/class_residual_ii.meta` — meta format reference (`id`/`targets`/`js.exit`/`js.check`).\n- `tests/conformance/src/lib.rs` — fixture discovery + `run_js` (compile → `emit_js` → `node -e` with appended `js.check`).\n- `third_party/test262/test/language/expressions/class/async-gen-method-static/dflt-params-arg-val-undefined.js` — canonical repro of the failing cluster.\n- `docs/adr/` — ADR 0007 (Test262 harness) relevant; ADR 0008/0009 locked platform decisions.",
