    "type": "text",
    "text": "## Objective\n- Execute one draconic-loop iteration: claim the next ROADMAP.md item, implement it test-first, mark it done only when `cargo test --workspace` is green, then stop without starting a second item.\n\n## Important Details\n- Claimed **T07** (`Negative typechecking`, `compiler` target) and split it into children **T07.01–T07.05**; T07 is `in_progress`, children are `todo`; this Loop completes only **T07.01** (annotated call-site argument checking: wrong arity and non-assignable args vs annotated params; untyped/unannotated params stay permissive).\n- Untyped JS must remain permissive (E19 mandate): enforcement only when the callee has annotated params.\n- Parser has **no function-type syntax** (`(x: number) => number` fails with `expected type name after ':'`) — enforcement must use the callee's own declared param annotations.\n- Reject fixtures work via `.meta` key `js.error: <substring>`; `run_all_fixtures_green_on_declared_targets` in `tests/conformance/tests/harness.rs` auto-discovers new fixtures.\n- Probe results (via `check_source`): **currently ACCEPTED** — wrong arg count, arg type mismatch, prop-assign mismatch, missing return, unknown prop on shape, call of non-function binding, excess prop literal, `i32` param called with string, `if` on union. **Currently REJECTED** — union→member, number→boolean, generic mismatch, alias/nested prop read mismatch, native→number return.\n- `require_assignable_expr` already handles number-literal→native and object/array-literal→shape contextual assignment.\n- Generic call checking exists (`instantiate_generic_call`, `Type::GenericFn`); non-generic declared functions are bare `Type::Function` with no recorded signature — needs a signature model or parallel table.\n- A temporary probe crate `crates/t07probe/` was added to workspace `Cargo.toml` members; it must be removed before `done`.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Read `CONTEXT.md` and `ROADMAP.md`.\n- ROADMAP edit: T07 → `in_progress`; added rows T07.01–T07.05.\n- Created and ran probe crate `crates/t07probe/` (added to workspace members) to map accept/reject gaps.\n- Investigated checker internals: `Type` enum (~109), `GenericFnSig` (139), `Checker` struct (2620: `symbol_types`, `symbol_annotated`, `shapes`, `generic_fns`, `expected_return`…), `check_expr` (3481), `Stmt::Let` check (3072), `instantiate_generic_call` (4579), `require_assignable_expr` (4785), `is_assignable` (4885), `prop_type` (4441, Shape/Intersection only; everything else falls back to `Type::Any`).\n- Confirmed frontend entry points: `check_source` / `check_source_module` at `crates/draconic-frontend/src/lib.rs:44/50`.\n- Confirmed parser maps `var` → `BindingKind::Var` (`crates/draconic-parser/src/lib.rs:2937`).\n- Noted `tests/conformance/fixtures/types/` currently contains only erase fixtures; no `types/reject/` directory yet.\n- Last commit: `1f4e596 E19.87`; branch main, ahead of origin/main by 45 commits; only untracked `.loop/logs/`.\n\n### Active\n- No red test fixtures written yet for T07.01.\n- No implementation changes made to `crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs` yet.\n- Temporary probe crate `crates/t07probe` still present in workspace.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write red tests: `tests/conformance/fixtures/types/reject/*.drac` + `*.meta` with `js.error` substrings covering: wrong arity (too few required; too many without rest; rest allows extras) and non-assignable arguments vs annotated params (incl. native and shape params); also green fixtures proving untyped/unannotated-param calls stay permissive.\n2. Implement annotated call-site argument checking in `crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs` — record param annotations for non-generic function declarations (extend signature model or add a `fn_sigs` table keyed by symbol id), enforce at `Expr::Call` / member-call sites via `require_assignable_expr` / `require_assignable`; skip enforcement when callee is unannotated/`Any`.\n3. Run `cargo test --workspace` until green; remove `crates/t07probe` and its workspace-member entry.\n4. Mark T07.01 `done` in `ROADMAP.md`; stop (do not start a second item).\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `ROADMAP.md`: T07 `in_progress`; T07.01–T07.05 rows; T07.01 is current Loop scope.\n- `crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs`: checker; `check_expr` ~3481, `Stmt::Let` 3072, `instantiate_generic_call` 4579, `require_assignable_expr` 4785, `is_assignable` 4885, `prop_type` 4441, `Checker` 2620, `GenericFnSig` 139, `Type` enum 109.\n- `crates/draconic-frontend/src/lib.rs`: `check_source` :44 / `check_source_module` :50 used by reject tests.\n- `tests/conformance/src/lib.rs`: fixture loader; `TargetExpect.error_contains`; `run_all`.\n- `tests/conformance/tests/types.rs`: T01–T06 test patterns (fixture-present + run assertions).\n- `tests/conformance/fixtures/types/`: erase fixtures; will hold `types/reject/` for T07.01.\n- `tests/conformance/fixtures/native/js-policy/ptr_hard_error.meta`: example of `js.error` reject-fixture meta.\n- `crates/t07probe/`: temporary probe crate (remove before done).\n- `Cargo.toml`: workspace members — includes `crates/t07probe` (revert before done).\n- `crates/draconic-parser/src/lib.rs`: `var` → `BindingKind::Var` at 2937.",
