    "text": "## Objective\n- Run the `draconic-loop` skill exactly once: claim the next `todo` ROADMAP.md item (T07.05), implement test-first, mark it `done` only when `cargo test --workspace` is green, then stop without starting a second item.\n\n## Important Details\n- `draconic-loop` rules: exactly one `in_progress` at a time; do not start E* clusters past B10 unless user overrides; prefer spine rows B/E/T/N/U over P/S; empty-todo guard = stop immediately; full Test262 suite is opt-in (`DRACONIC_TEST262_FULL` unset → smoke allowlist only).\n- Claimed item, ROADMAP.md row (verbatim):\n  `| T07.05 | todo | compiler | Object literal excess-property check vs annotated shape (e.g. `{a: 1, b: 2}` for `{a: number}`) → diagnostic | `tests/conformance` fixtures `types/reject` |`\n- Blockers satisfied: T07.01–T07.04 all `done`; repo on `main`, 49 commits ahead of `origin/main`, untracked `.loop/logs/`.\n- Recent commit pattern to mirror (e.g. `627bc27 T07.04`): ROADMAP.md row todo→done + `crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs` implementation + new `tests/conformance/fixtures/types/[...]` (.drac + .meta) + tests in `tests/conformance/tests/types.rs`; one commit per item.\n- Reject fixture convention: minimal `.drac` + `.meta` with `id:` / `targets: js` / `js.error: <needle substring>` (e.g. T07.03 uses `unknown property`, T07.04 uses `is not callable`); `expect_compile_or_emit_error` (tests/conformance/src/lib.rs:421) checks needle in compile-or-emit error.\n- Positive fixtures use `js.exit: 0` + `js.check: <node assertions>`; T07.04's positives: `call_annotated_callable_ok.drac`, `call_untyped_non_callable_ok.drac` (untyped stays permissive at runtime).\n- Code facts (crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs, 8709 lines):\n  - `ObjectShape { props: Vec<(String, Type)>, strict: bool }` (~line 168); `strict: true` only from `TypeAnn::Object` resolution (~line 4830 `intern_shape(shape_props, true)`); inferred object-literal shapes intern with `strict: false` (~line 4407 inference path).\n  - `require_assignable_expr` (~line 5082) has 7 call sites: 3253 (var init), 3616 (return), 3879 + 3960 (assign), 4391 (arrow body), 4540 (default), 5486 (call args).\n  - `object_literal_contextually_assignable` (~line 5113) only checks each target prop is present+assignable; it returns `false` on computed/spread/accessor, so an object literal with *extra* props currently passes contextual check → **that is the T07.05 gap**.\n  - Fresh-object-literal excess must reject only against `strict` shapes; variable-to-variable assignment (`let p = {a:1,b:2}; let q: {a:number} = p;`) must stay permissive (TypeScript semantics; `object_types_erase.drac` depends on this).\n  - AST: `ObjectProp::Property { key: ObjectKey, value: Expr, shorthand, span }` / `Accessor` / `Spread` (crates/draconic-ast/src/lib.rs:682); `ObjectKey::Ident | String | Computed` (:708); `StringLit.value` is `JsString`, existing code uses `s.value.to_string_lossy()` (:5124); `expr_span_of` helper at :5828.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Skill loaded; `ROADMAP.md` + `CONTEXT.md` read (truncated output; relevant rows at ROADMAP.md ~line 348 in the T07 block).\n- Oriented: inspected T07.01–T07.04 commits/diffs, `tests/conformance/tests/types.rs`, conformance harness (`load_fixtures`, `run_fixture`, `expect_compile_or_emit_error`), existing `types/` and `types/reject/` fixtures, and the checker's shape/assignability implementation.\n- Confirmed no existing `tests/conformance/types/` directory (fixtures live under `tests/conformance/fixtures/types/`).\n- Confirmed `annotated_call_ok.drac` (`useShape({ x: 1 })`) and `object_types_erase.drac` are positives that must keep passing.\n\n### Active\n- Orient phase finished; **Red step not yet started** — no fixtures/tests written, no implementation, no `cargo test` run, ROADMAP.md unchanged (T07.05 still `todo`).\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write Red fixtures:\n   - Rejects: `tests/conformance/fixtures/types/reject/object_literal_excess_prop.drac` (`let p: { a: number } = { a: 1, b: 2 };`) + `.meta` with `targets: js`, `js.error: excess property`; optionally string-key/shorthand variants (e.g. `{ a: 1, \"b\": 2 }`, `{ a: 1, b }`).\n   - Positives: exact-literal OK (`{ a: 1 }` for `{ a: number }`), extra-props-via-variable OK, unannotated-object OK — .drac + `.meta` with `js.exit: 0` / `js.check`.\n   - Add a unit test in `tests/conformance/tests/types.rs` calling `check()` directly asserting the excess-prop diagnostic, plus conformance fixture-run tests matching existing patterns.\n2. Implement Green in `crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs`: in `require_assignable_expr`/`object_literal_contextually_assignable` path, after target props pass, when `to_shape.strict` scan all object-literal `Property` keys (ident/string, honoring shorthand) and emit a diagnostic containing `\"excess property\"` for any name absent from the target shape; keep computed/spread/accessor handling permissive (return generic failure as today) and keep variable-assignment path untouched.\n3. Verify: `cargo test -p draconic-check -p draconic-conformance`, then `cargo test --workspace` (smoke allowlist).\n4. When green: set T07.05 to `done` in ROADMAP.md (same one-line `todo`→`done` edit pattern), commit, then stop — do not start another item.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `ROADMAP.md`: T07.05 row (~line 348) to claim/mark; source of truth.\n- `crates/draconic-check/src/lib.rs`: `ObjectShape` (:168), `intern_shape` (:4574), `require_assignable_expr` (:5082), `object_literal_contextually_assignable` (:5113), object-literal inference (:4407), `member_prop_type` (:4708, T07.03 precedent), `type_is_callable` (:5494, T07.04 precedent).\n- `tests/conformance/fixtures/types/`: positives (`annotated_call_ok.drac`, `object_types_erase.drac`, `call_annotated_callable_ok.drac`, `unknown_shape_prop_dynamic_ok.drac`).\n- `tests/conformance/fixtures/types/reject/`: T07.03/T07.04 reject fixture + `.meta` convention (`unknown_shape_prop_read.drac`, `call_non_callable_number.drac`, etc.).\n- `tests/conformance/tests/types.rs`: where T07 unit + fixture tests live.\n- `tests/conformance/src/lib.rs`: harness; `expect_compile_or_emit_error` (:421), `.meta` parsing (`js.error` :228).\n- `crates/draconic-ast/src/lib.rs`: `ObjectProp` (:682), `ObjectKey` (:708), `StringLit` (:815).",
