annel e2e (C01 + C02) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `concurrency/channels` |\n639: | C03 | todo | native | `once` / thread-safe init; mutex only if Runtime internals need it | `crates/draconic-runtime`, `tests/conformance` fixtures `concurrency/sync` |\n640: | C03.01 | todo | native | `once` / thread-safe init primitive | `crates/draconic-runtime`, `tests/conformance` fixtures `concurrency/sync` |\n641: | C03.02 | todo | native | Runtime-internal mutex only where required (not user-facing shared heap) | `crates/draconic-runtime` |\n642: | C04 | todo | compiler | Parallel `draconic test`: multi-fixture workers; deterministic aggregate exit | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n643: | C04.01 | todo | compiler | `draconic test` runs fixtures on worker pool (N>1) | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n644: | C04.02 | todo | compiler | Deterministic aggregate exit code + stable failure summary order | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n645: | C05 | todo | both | Structured cancellation / timeout helpers on async work (channels + timers) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `concurrency/cancel` |\n646: | C05.01 | todo | both | Cancel token / Abort-like signal: propagate to async work | `tests/conformance` fixtures `concurrency/cancel` |\n647: | C05.02 | todo | both | Timeout helper: race work vs timer (needs **H05**); settle cleanly | `tests/conformance` fixtures `concurrency/cancel` |\n648: | C06 | todo | native | Optional later: shared-memory atomics (advanced; not v1 bar) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `concurrency/atomics` |\n649: \n650: **C v1 done bar:** C01.01–03 + C02.01 + C02.04. C03/C04 tooling; C05 after H05; C06 later.\n651: \n652: **C critical path to worker+channel e2e:** C01.01 → C01.02 → C02.01 → C02.04.\n653: \n654: ---\n655: \n656: ## L — Stdlib libraries\n657: \n658: Portable libraries beyond raw host syscalls and ECMA builtins already under **E15** (JSON, RegExp — do not re-file). Prefer portable API + native Runtime impl; native-only must hard-error on js.\n659: \n660: | ID | Status | Targets | Item | Tests |\n661: |----|--------|---------|------|-------|\n662: | L01 | todo | both | Encoding: UTF-8 bytes↔string, Base64, hex | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/encoding` |\n663: | L01.01 | todo | both | UTF-8 encode/decode: string ↔ bytes; invalid UTF-8 error | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/encoding` |\n664: | L01.02 | todo | both | Base64 encode/decode | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/encoding` |\n665: | L01.03 | todo | both | Hex encode/decode | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/encoding` |\n666: | L02 | todo | both | Collections helpers (groupBy/chunk/Deque as designed; not redundant with Array/Map/Set) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/collections` |\n667: | L02.01 | todo | both | `groupBy` / `chunk` (or designed names) on arrays | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/collections` |\n668: | L02.02 | todo | both | Deque (or designed): push/pop both ends | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/collections` |\n669: | L03 | todo | both | Crypto: SHA-256 digest + secure random bytes | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/crypto` |\n670: | L03.01 | todo | both | SHA-256 digest over bytes; known test vectors | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/crypto` |\n671: | L03.02 | todo | both | Secure random bytes (OS CSPRNG); length parameter | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/crypto` |\n672: | L04 | todo | both | Compression later: gzip/deflate byte buffers | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/compression` |\n673: | L05 | todo | both | In-language test framework (`describe`/`it`/`expect` or designed) via `draconic test` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/testing`, `crates/draconic-cli` |\n674: | L05.01 | todo | both | `describe` / `it` (or designed) register tests; run via `draconic test` | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/testing`, `crates/draconic-cli` |\n675: | L05.02 | todo | both | `expect` matchers: equality, truthiness; failure messages | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/testing` |\n676: | L05.03 | todo | both | Nested describe; before/after hooks as designed | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/testing` |\n677: | L05.04 | todo | both | CLI aggregates in-language suite exit codes with fixture runner | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n678: | L06 | todo | both | Logging: leveled logger; stderr/stdout sink | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/logging` |\n679: | L06.01 | todo | both | Leveled log (error/warn/info/debug); filter by level | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/logging` |\n680: | L06.02 | todo | both | Sink to stderr/stdout (string format) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/logging` |\n681: | L07 | todo | both | Flags/CLI parse: argv → typed options/positionals | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/flags` |\n682: | L07.01 | todo | both | Parse long/short flags + positionals from string array | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/flags` |\n683: | L07.02 | todo | both | Typed options (bool/string/number); help text as designed | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/flags` |\n684: | L08 | todo | both | URL / query parse + serialize | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/url` |\n685: | L08.01 | todo | both | Parse URL: scheme/host/path/query/hash | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/url` |\n686: | L08.02 | todo | both | Query parse/serialize; round-trip common cases | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/url` |\n687: | L09 | todo | both | MIME multipart later (HTTP-shaped programs; after H10) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/mime` |\n688: | L10 | todo | both | Crypto later: HMAC + AEAD (after L03) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/crypto` |\n689: | L10.01 | todo | both | HMAC-SHA256 (after L03) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/crypto` |\n690: | L10.02 | todo | both | AEAD encrypt/decrypt (after L03; algorithm as designed) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `stdlib/crypto` |\n691: \n692: **L v1 done bar:** L01 + L03 + L05.01–02 + L06 + L08. L02/L07 polish; L04/L09/L10 later.\n693: \n694: **L critical path:** no ordered flagship; claim any v1-bar todo. Prefer L01/L03 before L10; L05 after U01.\n695: \n696: ---\n697: \n698: ## D — Distribution & install\n699: \n700: Ship the toolchain like rustup/go: installable binaries, pinned toolchain, multi-OS/arch.\n701: \n702: | ID | Status | Targets | Item | Tests |\n703: |----|--------|---------|------|-------|\n704: | D01 | todo | compiler | Release binaries + install script; one-line install to PATH | `tests/integration` (install smoke), CI |\n705: | D01.01 | todo | compiler | CI/release: produce platform binary artifact for host triple | CI, `tests/integration` |\n706: | D01.02 | todo | compiler | Install script: download + place `draconic` on PATH (one-line) | `tests/integration` (install smoke) |\n707: | D01.03 | todo | compiler | Install smoke: fresh PATH → `draconic -V` / parse hello | `tests/integration` |\n708: | D02 | todo | compiler | Toolchain version pin in `draconic.toml`; CLI enforces or warns | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n709: | D02.01 | todo | compiler | Manifest field: required/optional toolchain version | `crates/draconic-cli`, `crates/draconic-pkg` |\n710: | D02.02 | todo | compiler | CLI: enforce or warn when running toolchain ≠ pin | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n711: | D03 | todo | compiler | Reproducible builds: same source + pin → documented-equivalent artifacts | `tests/integration` |\n712: | D03.01 | todo | compiler | Document reproducibility expectations (timestamps, paths) | `tests/integration`, docs |\n713: | D03.02 | todo | compiler | Same source + pin → byte-identical or documented-equivalent emit | `tests/integration` |\n714: | D04 | todo | native | Cross-compile matrix: linux/darwin/windows × amd64/arm64 (as available) | `tests/integration`, `crates/draconic-backend-llvm` |\n715: | D04.01 | todo | native | Cross-compile: at least one non-host triple smoke | `tests/integration`, `crates/draconic-backend-llvm` |\n716: | D04.02 | todo | native | Matrix docs + CI jobs for available OS/arch pairs | CI, `tests/integration` |\n717: | D05 | todo | native | Binary size opts: strip / LTO flags documented and testable | `tests/integration`, `crates/draconic-cli` |\n718: | D05.01 | todo | native | CLI/build flags: strip symbols | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n719: | D05.02 | todo | native | LTO (or designed) flag documented; size delta smoke | `crates/draconic-cli`, `tests/integration` |\n720: \n721: **D v1 done bar:** D01.01–03 + D02. D03/D04/D05 deepen distribution quality.\n722: \n723: **D critical path to installable toolchain:** D01.01 → D01.02 → D01.03 → D02.01–02.\n724: \n725: ---\n726: \n727: ## R — Reliability, security, sandbox\n728: \n729: Embed/runtime safety, optional permissions, supply-chain (with **K**), native failure policy. Does not replace **N09** GC stress or **N07** embed surface.\n730: \n731: | ID | Status | Targets | Item | Tests |\n732: |----|--------|---------|------|-------|\n733: | R01 | todo | native | Embed/eval resource limits: max source size, alloc/time budget | `crates/draconic-embed`, `crates/draconic-runtime` |\n734: | R01.01 | todo | native | Max source size for embed/eval; reject oversize | `crates/draconic-embed` |\n735: | R01.02 | todo | native | Alloc budget: fail closed when exceeded | `crates/draconic-runtime`, `crates/draconic-embed` |\n736: | R01.03 | todo | native | Time budget: interrupt/fail long-running eval | `crates/draconic-embed`, `crates/draconic-runtime` |\n737: | R02 | todo | both | Permission model (optional Deno-like): grant/deny fs and net; clear deny diagnostics | `tests/conformance` fixtures `security/permissions` |\n738: | R02.01 | todo | both | Permission grants: fs read/write, net listen/connect (as designed) | `tests/conformance` fixtures `security/permissions` |\n739: | R02.02 | todo | both | Deny path: clear diagnostic when host op lacks grant | `tests/conformance` fixtures `security/permissions` |\n740: | R02.03 |